{"seq":2,"slug":"a-recluse-by-choice","title":"A Recluse By Choice","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/life-and-times/a-recluse-by-choice","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"refusing-the-prime-minister","title":"拒绝相位","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/life-and-times/a-recluse-by-choice/refusing-the-prime-minister","wordCount":1666,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"poverty-and-freedom","title":"清贫与自由","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/life-and-times/a-recluse-by-choice/poverty-and-freedom","wordCount":1655,"readingTime":7}],"introHtml":"<p>本章呈现庄子超越功名、追求自由的人生选择。面对楚王以相位的礼聘，庄子断然拒绝，以&quot;曳尾于涂中&quot;的比喻，表明宁愿在卑微中保全自由的生命，也不愿为显赫的功名而牺牲精神的自由。他选择了清贫的隐居生活，却在清贫中获得了精神的逍遥。本章揭示庄子&quot;清贫与自由&quot;深刻统一的人生境界。</p>\n"}